# The preview serves the College, and only the College.
#
# There is no build step on Vercel: scripts/build-madinah.js has already run
# and its output — the 32 index.html files, the sitemap — is committed. So
# Vercel is a static host here, and everything it does not need to SERVE is
# withheld rather than uploaded and then left reachable.
#
# The first deployment kept scripts/ and madinah-src/ because I assumed the
# build would run on Vercel. It did not need to, and the result was that the
# page templates and the generator were both fetchable on the preview domain:
# /madinah-src/manifest.json and /scripts/build-madinah.js each returned 200.
archive/
docs/
tests/
sql/
scripts/
madinah-src/
.claude/
*.md

# Stray screenshot output from a verification harness. Never part of the site.
undefined/

# The consent register names real people and records what they said. It is a
# governance record, not a page. It was reachable at
# /assets/photography/licence-register.tsv on the first deployment; it is not
# to be served again. The same goes for the slot table beside it.
assets/photography/licence-register.tsv
assets/photography/README.md

# The OFL asks that the licence travel with the font. It does.
!assets/fonts/LICENCE.md
